export const clientTermsAndConditions = `MULTIVENT
CLIENT TERMS & CONDITIONS

Version 1.1 | Draft date: 31 October 2026 | Effective date: To be assigned upon publication

Academic project draft — reviewed legal references are embedded at the relevant clauses; this is not legal clearance for commercial use.

1. Introduction and Scope
MULTIVENT is an academic capstone project for a mobile-based event-planning platform. Its current pilot focuses on wedding services in Bacolod City, Philippines. These Client Terms & Conditions govern access, accounts, inquiries, bookings, payments, communications and use of the platform. They must be read with the Privacy Policy and the Cancellation, Rescheduling, No-Show, and Refund Policy.

2. Electronic Acceptance and Agreement
By affirmatively accepting these Terms and submitting a booking, the Client agrees to the applicable platform rules and confirmed service conditions. MULTIVENT should record the accepted version and timestamp; merely viewing a page is not by itself treated as express booking acceptance.

3. Eligibility
The platform is intended for Clients who are at least eighteen (18) years old and capable of entering into agreements. Where an event concerns minors, an appropriate adult is responsible for the booking and must avoid submitting unnecessary personal information about them.

4. Client Accounts and Security
Clients must provide accurate registration details, protect their credentials, and report suspected unauthorized activity. Account information is processed in accordance with the Data Privacy Act of 2012.

5. Platform Role and Legal Responsibilities
MULTIVENT facilitates discovery, comparison, booking coordination, messaging and related platform processes. Independent Service Providers perform the actual event services. This distinction does not eliminate duties imposed on an e-marketplace or digital platform by applicable law.

6. Service Listings and Provider Information
Clients may review listed service names, categories, prices, descriptions, package inclusions, conditions and availability. Providers are responsible for accurate listings, while MULTIVENT exercises applicable platform diligence.

7. Booking, Acceptance and Confirmation
When a Client selects multiple Service Providers for one event, every required provider must accept its respective request before payment. A request or an isolated provider acceptance is not a Confirmed booking. Confirmation occurs only after all required acceptances and the required successful payment or downpayment are recorded.

8. Payment Deadline
After all required providers have accepted, the Client ordinarily has seven (7) calendar days to make the required payment. A shorter deadline may apply if the event occurs earlier. An unpaid request may expire and availability may be released.

9. Client-Facing Pricing and Five Percent Markup
MULTIVENT applies a five percent (5%) markup to the applicable provider base price. It is ordinarily embedded in the displayed Client-facing service price. Before confirming, the Client must see the accurate total payable and any additional applicable charges.

10. Payment and Downpayment Options
MULTIVENT may present full-payment or percentage-based downpayment options after provider acceptance. The required percentage, amount due now and balance must be displayed in the transaction summary. A booking becomes Confirmed only when its required payment is successfully recorded.

11. Capstone Payment Simulation
PayMongo is currently integrated for simulated/test payments. Test records illustrate payment status, booking confirmation and ledger logic; they do not constitute actual money collection, escrow, disbursement or financial settlement.

12. Remaining Balance After Event
When the downpayment option applies, the remaining agreed service balance is settled directly by the Client to each relevant Service Provider after the event. The provider must acknowledge receipt and issue appropriate documentation where required.

13. Event Information and Good-Faith Cooperation
Clients must submit accurate event dates, locations, guest counts, requirements and contact details, and promptly disclose material changes. False or knowingly misleading booking details may justify investigation and proportionate account restrictions.

14. Instructions and Custom Requests
Clients may provide instructions through each provider's instruction or messaging module. A request does not automatically amend a confirmed service; material changes to price, scope, date or deliverables require clear acceptance by the Service Provider.

15. Cancellations, Refunds and Rescheduling
The Cancellation, Rescheduling, No-Show, and Refund Policy controls ordinary voluntary Client cancellations: 30 or more days before the event, 100% of the eligible booking amount; 15–29 days, 50%; fewer than 15 days, non-refundable. One no-fee rescheduling request is permitted, subject to provider availability.

16. Individual Services and Preset Packages
A booking with one provider may normally be cancelled without automatically cancelling other providers in the event. A predefined package is ordinarily one indivisible booking unit.

17. Messaging and Professional Conduct
Messaging and sharing contact information for genuine booking coordination are permitted. Important booking amendments, cancellations and disputes should be documented in MULTIVENT. Threats, harassment, spam, fraud and misuse of another person's private information are prohibited.

18. Event Coordinator Access
A booked Event Coordinator may access only event information expressly authorized and technically permitted for that engagement. A coordinator is not an Administrator and shall not receive unrelated bookings, private financial credentials or broader account access.

19. Reviews, Complaints and Ratings
Ratings and public service reviews are reserved for Completed bookings. Cancelled or undelivered services are addressed through incident reports or complaints. Reviews must reflect genuine experiences.

20. Recommendations and AI-Generated Insights
Recommendations and AI-generated insights are decision-support aids, not guarantees. Personal information used for these features must be handled lawfully, proportionately and securely.

21. Privacy and Data Subject Rights
The separate MULTIVENT Privacy Policy governs collection, sharing, retention, processing and rights procedures. Clients retain applicable rights to be informed, access and correct information, and request erasure or blocking in legally qualifying cases.

22. Prohibited Acts and Security
Fraudulent accounts, fake bookings or refunds, harassment, unauthorized system access, malicious uploads, misleading reviews and attempts to compromise platform security are prohibited. MULTIVENT may take proportionate preventive action, including temporary restrictions or suspension.

23. Suspension, Account Closure and Appeals
Accounts may be restricted or terminated for justified violations, with an opportunity for review where appropriate. Account deletion does not extinguish accrued booking, payment, refund or legal obligations.

24. System Maintenance and Transaction Errors
MULTIVENT may experience outages and correct genuine errors in price, availability or records. Confirmed transactions affected by an error should be resolved transparently with notice and appropriate remedy.

25. Complaints and Internal Redress
Complaints may be submitted through MULTIVENT Help and Support and reviewed using relevant records and evidence. This does not replace competent government or judicial remedies.

26. Independent Service Provider and Platform Liability
Service Providers perform the advertised event services; MULTIVENT remains accountable for its own platform conduct and statutory duties. Broad disclaimers cannot override applicable law.

27. Content and Intellectual Property
Clients retain rights in material they lawfully submit and authorize MULTIVENT to process or display it as reasonably necessary for the platform. Uploaded material must not violate others' rights or privacy.

28. Updates and Version Control
Material changes to these Terms should be communicated with renewed acknowledgment where needed. A confirmed booking ordinarily remains subject to the version accepted at confirmation unless validly changed or required otherwise by law.

29. Governing Law and Reservation of Rights
These Terms are governed by applicable Philippine law. No clause is intended to waive nonwaivable rights under applicable statutes.

30. Contact and Assistance
Current support route: in-app Help and Support. Official support and privacy contact information must be established before public deployment.

31. Client Acknowledgment
By creating an account, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to the MULTIVENT Client Terms & Conditions and acknowledge the MULTIVENT Privacy Policy. Optional marketing consent, if implemented, must be separate.`

